NickelOS: an Android app launched while Android isn't running starts the
session in the background, so only the app's own window opens. Waydroid
started it in the foreground: Android's whole UI came up first in a window
of its own with no app id or title (a nameless cube on the shelf), and the
app opened inside it.

--- a/tools/actions/app_manager.py	2026-05-28 20:02:24.000000000 +0000
+++ b/tools/actions/app_manager.py	2026-10-20 00:41:20.462130540 +0000
@@ -69,7 +69,7 @@
         launchNow()
     except dbus.DBusException:
         logging.error("Starting waydroid session")
-        tools.actions.session_manager.start(args, launchNow, background=False)
+        tools.actions.session_manager.start(args, launchNow, background=True)
 
 def launch(args):
     def justLaunch():
